    "body": "Closes #109.\n\nImplements ADR-011 end-to-end: the browser now renders HTML pages to pixels. Five commits.\n\n## What you will see\n\nLaunch `./build/bin/honeybee` and the view area shows:\n\n- **HoneyBee Browser** — 32px, orange (#d35400)\n- **Version 0.1.0**\n- **Type a URL above and press Enter to load a page.**\n- **هذا نص عربي. Rendered via Pango for correct shaping.**\n\nArabic renders with **connected letterforms** (correct shaping), not isolated characters — Pango is doing its job.\n\nType `https://example.com` in the URL bar and press Enter: the full pipeline runs, and the page body is rendered by our own layout and paint code.\n\n## The five commits\n\n**1. `feat(layout)` — block-flow layout + box model parsing**\n- `renderer/layout/`: `LayoutBox`, `LayoutText`, `LayoutNode` (abstract base), `Color`, `TextMeasurer`\n- Recursive pre-order block flow, box model applied margin -> border -> padding -> content\n- Width fills parent; height derived from children\n- `TextMeasurer` seam: production uses Pango, tests use a fake (chars * 8 x 16) — fully testable without GTK\n- 16 tests including the exact worked example from ADR-011's ASCII diagram (y=10 / y=46)\n\n**2. `feat(paint)` — Cairo paint stage**\n- `renderer/paint/`: walks the layout tree, fills backgrounds, draws four border strips, invokes a `TextDrawer` callback per text node\n- Takes raw `cairo_t*`, injected `TextDrawer` — headless testable via `cairo_image_surface_t`\n- 7 tests with pixel-level verification (red at center, white outside)\n\n**3. `feat(layout)` — skip non-rendered elements**\n- Hardcoded skip list for `head`, `style`, `script`, `title`, `meta`, `link`, `base`\n- Found during manual testing: CSS source text was leaking into the visible page because block flow treats every element as visible\n- 3 regression tests\n\n**4. `feat(browser)` — wire the pipeline into the window**\n- `src/browser/pango_text.{hpp,cpp}` — Pango-backed `TextMeasurer` and `TextDrawer` (offline 1x1 image surface for measurement; `pango_cairo_show_layout` for correct Arabic shaping)\n- `src/browser/render_pipeline.{hpp,cpp}` — owns the DOM and layout tree, runs `html::parse -> extract_inline_css -> cascade -> layout`\n- `window.{hpp,cpp}` — `Gtk::Label` replaced by `Gtk::DrawingArea`; new `on_draw` and `render_html` methods; welcome page rendered on startup\n- CMake: `pango_text.cpp` and `render_pipeline.cpp` go into the `honeybee` executable, not `honeybee_lib` — the lib stays GTK/Pango-free for headless CI\n\n**5. `docs(adr)` — ADR-011 implementation notes**\n- Records five C++-surface deviations from the written spec, none architectural:\n  - `LayoutNode` is abstract base, not `std::variant`\n  - `paint()` takes `cairo_t*`, not `Cairo::RefPtr`\n  - `TextDrawer` seam (analogous to `TextMeasurer`)\n  - Non-rendered element skip list (temporary, pending UA stylesheet)\n  - Inline `<style>` extraction lives in `render_pipeline.cpp`\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests` -> **130 cases, 527 assertions, all pass** (was 104 before this branch)\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[layout]\"` -> **19 cases, 71 assertions**\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[paint]\"` -> **7 cases, 13 assertions**\n- `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp` — ADR-007 isolation holds\n- Headless test binary stays GTK/Pango-free — CI runs clean on a machine without a display server\n\n## Manual visual test\n\nLoaded the welcome page and typed `https://example.com` in the URL bar. Both render correctly:\n- Welcome page shows the four expected lines, Arabic letterforms connected\n- Example.com shows the heading and paragraph, styled by the CSS in the page\n\n## Screenshot\n\nA screenshot of the running window will be attached as a PR comment. It's the artifact that proves the ADR chain from #91 through #108 renders a real page.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-011)\n\nInline formatting, text wrapping, margin collapse, floats, flexbox, grid, positioning, overflow/scroll, images, tables, UA stylesheet, typed `Length`/`Color` values, bidi direction propagation from `dir=\"rtl\"`.\n\n## Next\n\nWith the first paint landed, the natural next ADRs are:\n- **UA stylesheet**: `<h1>` at 2em, `<body>` margin 8px, `<em>` italic, etc. Small but high-leverage\n- **Inline formatting**: `<span>`, `<a>`, `<em>`, text wrapping — needed for real pages\n- **Shorthand expansion**: `margin: 10px 20px` (currently defaults to 0)\n\nEach will be its own ADR + issue + PR, same rhythm.\n",
